Hi, I've been trying to debug a strange behavior of my QCA6174 for a
few weeks now, with no luck.
Right now I'm using kernel 5.8.10, with latest ath10k firmware from
Kalle Valo's github repository,
and I'm facing the current issue: I'm connected to an AP with 5GHz
Wi-Fi, on this network there are two more devices connected, always on
5GHz. Now, everything works fine, until I also connect a particular
Huawei smartphone to the same AP. When that happens,
I start to continuously lose connection, from the logs it looks like
that the card doesn't send packets  anymore, in fact I see a long list
of `htt tx alloc msdu_id` with no corresponding `htt tx free msdu_id`,
also there is no log regarding `tx completed` and no log regarding
`rx` events.

When I lose connection, the wireless card still reports that it is
connected to the AP, but from Wireshark I see that it starts sending A
LOT of ARP messages asking `Who's got _GATEWAY ADDRESS_ tell _my
address_`, but I don't think they get actually delivered, because
after some time the ksoftirqd process starts to consume a lot of
memory and a lot of cpu.

During the wifi blackout,
If I run `iw dev wlp2s0 scan`, I get connection timed out.
If I run `iw dev wlp2s0 scan` a second time, I get resource
temporarily unavailable
If I run `iw dev wlp2s0 scan` a third time, the scan successfully
happens and the network is back working (not for long though).

During these commands in the kernel logs I see that the hardware is restarted.

Now, I this it's worth nothing that with kernel 4.15 I didn't have
this issue, and that the firmware does not seem to be the problem per
se, because I tested all firmwares  with 4.15, 4.19 and 5.8 kernels.
With 4.15 I never get this bug, starting from 4.19 the bug is always happening.

I noticed that from 4.19 you changed the tx queue implementation, so
that's a possible cause.
I could not determine any other problem, I don't really know what to
do, what do you suggest?

I'll add some logs of the ath10k driver, the last part of which is
printed while the bug happens.

Thanks in advance for the help,
Greetings, F. M.

